\refstepcounter{section}
\begin{theorem}[Mantel]
If a finite simple graph $G$ on $n$ vertices contains no triangle, then $|E(G)|\le\lfloor n^2/4\rfloor$.
\end{theorem}
Triangle-free is expressed by nonexistence of an embedding of $K_3$. The empty and singleton cases are included. The independent solution uses degree sums and Cauchy--Schwarz; the proctor upper bound specializes the general Turán theorem \cite{MathlibTuran} to forbidden triangles.
